r"""
Superpowers plugin — self-contained snapshot (v6.1.1).

This single file embeds the ENTIRE superpowers plugin tree (skills, hooks,
agents, docs, everything) as base64. Running it recreates that tree, relative
to your current working directory, into the folder Claude Code loads plugins
from "in place" (no marketplace, no network, no install step).

HOW TO PORT IT ONTO A NEW MACBOOK
---------------------------------
Requirement: Python 3 only (pure standard library — no pip installs).

1. Create the target plugin folder and cd into it. The folder name
   ("superpowers") becomes the plugin name. Do NOT run this from ~/.claude
   itself — it must be its own dedicated subfolder:

       mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills/superpowers
       cd ~/.claude/skills/superpowers

2. Run THIS file from inside that folder. It rebuilds the whole tree there
   (creates ./.claude-plugin/plugin.json, ./skills/, ./hooks/, ...):

       python3 /path/to/summary.py

3. Restore executable bits. This script writes every file as plain data
   (mode 0644), so scripts lose their +x. Fix the ones Claude runs:

       # every script that starts with a shebang (#!):
       find . -type f -exec sh -c 'head -c2 "$1" | grep -q "#!" && chmod +x "$1"' _ {} \;
       # the hook launcher is a polyglot with NO shebang, so chmod it explicitly:
       chmod +x hooks/run-hook.cmd

4. Restart Claude Code (the SessionStart hook only wires on a fresh session).

VERIFY
------
   - `/plugin`  (or `claude plugin list`) should show:  superpowers@skills-dir
   - New sessions should begin with the "you have superpowers" injection.

WHY THIS LOCATION
-----------------
Per the Claude Code plugins reference: any folder under a skills directory
(~/.claude/skills/ or a project .claude/skills/) that contains a
.claude-plugin/plugin.json manifest is loaded as a plugin "<name>@skills-dir"
on the next session — discovered in place, with no marketplace and no install
step. Because the plugin ships its own hooks/hooks.json (a SessionStart hook),
you do NOT need to touch ~/.claude/settings.json — the hook activates with the
plugin. Do not, by contrast, hand-copy this into ~/.claude/plugins/cache/... :
that path is only recognized via installed_plugins.json registration entries
and will be ignored if populated by hand.

NOTES / GOTCHAS
---------------
   - Run from a DEDICATED empty subfolder. Paths here are relative and overwrite
     matching files in the cwd, so an empty ~/.claude/skills/superpowers/ is safe.
   - Don't ALSO scatter the individual skills loose under ~/.claude/skills/ —
     this plugin folder already provides them; doing both duplicates every skill.
"""
